{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1501214-a-couple-of-questions-metal-men-negotiating-with-trolls","id":1501214,"title":"A couple of Questions: Metal Men & Negotiating With Trolls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-23T22:55:44-08:00","id":1501214,"title":"A couple of Questions: Metal Men & Negotiating With Trolls","content":"In Norse Mythology are there any instances of metal men? Or made of stone also works.<br /> Also, how do the characters in Norse myth typically talk to or negotiate with trolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T23:57:56-08:00","id":1501376,"title":"","content":"Well there's Hrungnir, who was a jotunn said to be made of stone. Thor eventually kills him but that doesn't mean that Hrungnir is the only one of his line (or only jotunn made of stone). I can't think of another example of a stone or metal man off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Trolls are largely considered to be antagonists in Norse mythology but the gods might speak with them. Jotnar, in Norse legend, can be friendly and allies (Skadi and Gerd for two good examples) as well as being adversaries. Trolls seem to be represented as &quot;generally not helpful or friendly&quot; and I can't right away think of or find an example to the contrary of a friendly or at least friendly-leaning troll but I don't imagine that every meeting is immediately a violent or antagonistic one, so long as one considers their generally &quot;unhelpful&quot; demeanor and has something that mig